# Qwen2.5-VL 3B with a context window large enough for a sampled frame set.
#
# Ollama defaults this model to a 4096-token context. That is not enough: a single
# video's frames dominate the prompt, and at FRAME_MAX_LONG_EDGE=768 each frame
# costs roughly 1,250 tokens. Six frames plus the taxonomy prompt already measured
# 7,655 tokens, and the corpus reaches 12 frames on longer videos:
#
#   frames   approx. prompt tokens at 768px long edge
#   ------   ----------------------------------------
#        6   ~7,700
#        8   ~10,200
#       12   ~15,200
#       16   ~20,200   (MAX_ANALYSIS_FRAMES ceiling)
#
# 16384 covers the corpus as configured. Raising it further costs VRAM for KV
# cache, which is the binding constraint on a 6 GB card - see ARCHITECTURE.md
# "Local vs rented inference".
#
# Build:
#   ollama create qwen2.5vl-3b-16k -f ollama/Modelfile.qwen2.5vl-3b-16k

FROM qwen2.5vl:3b

PARAMETER num_ctx 16384

# Deterministic output: the same frames must produce the same tags across runs,
# otherwise the benchmark measures sampling noise rather than model quality.
PARAMETER temperature 0
PARAMETER top_p 1
PARAMETER seed 42
